@startuml Contract-Order State Machine v2 - Early Order Creation
!theme vibrant
skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam roundcorner 15
skinparam state {
  BackgroundColor<<Initial>> #E8F5E9
  BackgroundColor<<Processing>> #FFF3E0
  BackgroundColor<<Waiting>> #E3F2FD
  BackgroundColor<<Success>> #C8E6C9
  BackgroundColor<<Error>> #FFCDD2
  BackgroundColor<<Contract>> #F3E5F5
  BackgroundColor<<Order>> #E1F5FE
  BorderColor #455A64
  FontSize 12
}

title Contract-Order State Machine v2\n(Early Order Creation Pattern)

note as N_LEGEND
  **Key Change from v1:**

  Order is now created EARLY in the flow,
  right after CONTRACT_DRAFT completes.

  **New Flow:**
  CONTRACT_DRAFT -> NOT_FINISHED -> CONTRACT_PENDING

  **Benefits:**
  - Order number assigned early
  - Order visible in admin immediately
  - Customer has order reference during payment
end note

[*] --> BASKET_ACTIVE : User adds items

state BASKET_ACTIVE <<Initial>>
note right of BASKET_ACTIVE
  **Shopping Phase:**
  - User browsing, adding items
  - No contract yet
  - No order yet
  - Basket in session
end note

BASKET_ACTIVE --> CONTRACT_DRAFT : **Event:** CheckoutInitiatedEvent\n(User clicks "Place Order")

note as N_PHASE1
  **PHASE 1: CONTRACT DRAFT**
  Contract created, basket snapshotted
end note

state CONTRACT_DRAFT <<Contract>> {
  state "CONTRACT: DRAFT\n(Intent captured,\nconditions defined)" as CD

  note right of CD
    **Contract Created:**

    Contract record in database:
    - OXSTATE = 'draft'
    - OXORDERID = NULL (no order yet)
    - OXBASKETDATA = {snapshot}
    - OXCONDITIONS = [
        {type: 'payment_authorized', status: 'pending'},
        {type: 'fraud_check', status: 'pending'},
        {type: 'stock_reserved', status: 'pending'}
      ]

    **What happens:**
    1. Basket snapshot captured (immutable)
    2. Conditions defined
    3. Contract saved to osc_payment_contract
  end note
}

CONTRACT_DRAFT --> NOT_FINISHED : **Event:** ContractDraftCompletedEvent\n(Draft complete, create order)

note on link
  **NEW: Early Order Creation**

  Order is created immediately after
  contract draft is complete.

  This ensures:
  - Order number is assigned early
  - Order is visible in admin
  - Customer has reference number
end note

note as N_PHASE2
  **PHASE 2: ORDER CREATED (NOT_FINISHED)**
  Order exists but payment not yet processed
end note

state NOT_FINISHED <<Order>> {
  state "ORDER: NOT_FINISHED\n(Order created,\nawaiting payment processing)" as NF

  note right of NF
    **Order Created Early:**

    Database state:
    - oxorder.OXID exists
    - oxorder.oxordernr assigned
    - oxorder.oxtransstatus = 'NOT_FINISHED'
    - Contract.OXORDERID = order.OXID
    - Contract.OXSTATE = 'not_finished'

    **Order is now:**
    - Visible in admin
    - Has order number
    - Linked to contract

    **Payment conditions:**
    Still being resolved in parallel
  end note
}

NF : **Contract-Order Link Established**
NF : Contract.OXORDERID -> Order.OXID

NOT_FINISHED --> CONTRACT_PENDING : **Event:** OrderCreatedEvent\n(Proceed to payment processing)

note as N_PHASE3
  **PHASE 3: CONTRACT PENDING**
  Payment conditions being resolved
end note

state CONTRACT_PENDING <<Contract>> {
  state "CONTRACT: PENDING\n(Conditions being resolved)" as CP

  note right of CP
    **Parallel Condition Resolution:**

    Multiple handlers work in parallel:

    +-- PaymentAuthorizationHandler
    |   -> Calls provider API
    |   -> Fulfills 'payment_authorized'
    |
    +-- FraudCheckHandler
    |   -> Runs fraud detection
    |   -> Fulfills 'fraud_check'
    |
    +-- StockReservationHandler
        -> Reserves inventory
        -> Fulfills 'stock_reserved'

    Contract monitors:
    Are ALL conditions fulfilled?
  end note
}

CP : **State in DB:**
CP : Contract.OXSTATE = 'pending'
CP : Contract.OXORDERID = order.OXID
CP : OXCONDITIONS = [conditions being resolved...]

CONTRACT_PENDING --> CONTRACT_READY : **Event:** ContractConditionsFulfilledEvent\n(All conditions met)

note on link
  **Critical Transition:**

  Contract detected all conditions
  are now fulfilled.

  Contract automatically transitions
  to READY_TO_COMMIT state.
end note

CONTRACT_PENDING --> CONTRACT_FAILED : **Event:** ContractFailedEvent\n(Condition failed)

note on link
  **Failure Scenarios:**
  - Payment declined
  - Fraud detected
  - Stock unavailable

  Order marked as cancelled
  Contract state = 'failed'
end note

state CONTRACT_READY <<Contract>> {
  state "CONTRACT: READY_TO_COMMIT\n(All conditions met,\nready for commitment)" as CR

  note right of CR
    **Ready for Commitment:**

    All conditions fulfilled:
    v Payment authorized
    v Fraud check passed
    v Stock reserved

    Contract state:
    - OXSTATE = 'ready_to_commit'
    - OXORDERID = order.OXID
    - OXCONDITIONS = [all fulfilled]

    **Next:** Commit contract
  end note
}

CR : **Optimal Commitment Point**
CR : All risks mitigated

note as N_PHASE4
  **PHASE 4: CONTRACT COMMITTED**
  Contract committed, payment can be captured
end note

CONTRACT_READY --> CONTRACT_COMMITTED : **Event:** ContractReadyToCommitEvent\n(Auto-commit or manual)

state CONTRACT_COMMITTED <<Contract>> {
  state "CONTRACT: COMMITTED\n(Payment authorized,\nready for capture)" as CC

  note right of CC
    **Contract Committed:**

    Database state:
    - Contract.OXSTATE = 'committed'
    - Contract.OXORDERID = order.OXID
    - Order.oxtransstatus = 'NOT_FINISHED'

    **Payment authorized, capture pending!**

    **From here, external events:**
    - PaymentInitiatedEvent (redirect to provider)
    - OrderCancelledEvent (user/admin cancellation)
  end note
}

CC : **External Events Can Occur**
CC : (Beyond this ticket's scope)

CONTRACT_COMMITTED --> IN_PROGRESS : **Event:** PaymentInitiatedEvent\n(Redirect to provider)

CONTRACT_COMMITTED --> CONTRACT_CANCELLED : **Event:** OrderCancelledEvent\n(External cancellation)

note on link
  **External Events:**

  Beyond this ticket's scope.
  Either PaymentInitiatedEvent or
  OrderCancelledEvent can be emitted
  by external systems.
end note

state IN_PROGRESS <<Processing>> {
  state "IN_PROGRESS\n(500-800)\nPayment Processing\nat Provider" as IP

  state IP {
    state "500\nExternal Payment" as EP
    state "700\nCard Payment" as CardPay
    state "750\nCard Authorized" as CA
    state "800\nNeed Finalization" as NF2

    [*] --> EP : Redirect payment
    [*] --> CardPay : Card payment
    CardPay --> CA : Authorized
    CA --> NF2 : Finalize
  }

  note right of IP
    **Order Processing States:**

    500 - External (iDEAL, EPS, etc.)
    700 - Card processing (3DS)
    750 - Card authorized
    800 - Need finalization

    **Contract state:**
    Still COMMITTED (waiting for capture)
  end note
}

IN_PROGRESS --> AWAITING_WEBHOOK : **Event:** PaymentApprovedEvent\n(Customer return)

state AWAITING_WEBHOOK <<Waiting>> {
  state "AWAITING_WEBHOOK\n(600)\nWaiting for Provider\nWebhook Confirmation" as AW

  note right of AW
    **Webhook Pending:**

    Customer completed payment at provider,
    now awaiting async webhook confirmation.

    **Contract state:**
    Still COMMITTED (capture pending)

    **Order state:**
    AWAITING_WEBHOOK (600)

    Timeout: 60 minutes
  end note
}

AWAITING_WEBHOOK --> CONTRACT_FULFILLED : **Event:** PaymentCapturedEvent\n(Webhook received)

note on link
  **Webhook Processing:**

  WebhookHandler:
  1. Finds contract by provider order ID
  2. Verifies contract state = COMMITTED
  3. Calls contract.fulfill()
  4. Updates order to OK
  5. Emits ContractFulfilledEvent
end note

IN_PROGRESS --> CONTRACT_FULFILLED : **Event:** PaymentCapturedEvent\n(Direct capture)

note on link
  Some payment flows
  capture directly without
  webhook waiting period
end note

state CONTRACT_FULFILLED <<Success>> {
  state "CONTRACT: FULFILLED\n(Payment captured,\ncontract complete)" as CF

  note right of CF
    **Contract Fulfilled:**

    Database state:
    - Contract.OXSTATE = 'fulfilled'
    - Contract.OXFULFILLEDAT = NOW()
    - Order.oxpaid = NOW()
    - Order.oxtransstatus = 'OK'

    **Contract lifecycle complete!**

    Side effects triggered:
    - Email confirmation
    - Inventory update
    - Invoice generation
    - Analytics tracking
  end note
}

CF : **Terminal Success State**

CONTRACT_FULFILLED --> COMPLETED : Order finalized

state COMPLETED <<Success>> {
  state "ORDER: COMPLETED\n(OK)\nOrder Ready for\nFulfillment/Shipping" as SUCCESS

  note right of SUCCESS
    **Order Completed:**

    Final state:
    - Order.oxtransstatus = 'OK'
    - Order.oxpaid = timestamp
    - Contract.OXSTATE = 'fulfilled'

    **Ready for:**
    - Shipment processing
    - Invoice generation
    - Customer service
  end note
}

COMPLETED --> [*]

note as N_PHASE5
  **PHASE 5: ERROR & CANCELLATION PATHS**
  Handling failures and cancellations
end note

CONTRACT_FAILED --> CONTRACT_CANCELLED : Contract cancelled

state CONTRACT_FAILED <<Error>> {
  state "CONTRACT: FAILED\n(Condition failed)" as CFail

  note right of CFail
    **Contract Failed:**

    Reasons:
    - Payment declined
    - Fraud detected (high risk)
    - Stock unavailable
    - Address validation failed

    Contract state:
    - OXSTATE = 'failed'
    - OXSTATEREASON = "reason"
    - OXORDERID = order.OXID (order exists!)

    **Order marked as cancelled**
  end note
}

state CONTRACT_CANCELLED <<Error>> {
  state "CANCELLED\n(Contract/Order cancelled)" as CANCEL

  note right of CANCEL
    **Cancellation:**

    Order and contract both cancelled:
    - Contract.OXSTATE = 'cancelled'
    - Order.OXSTORNO = 1

    Clean cancellation with full audit trail
  end note
}

NOT_FINISHED --> CONTRACT_CANCELLED : **Event:** OrderCancelledEvent
IN_PROGRESS --> CONTRACT_CANCELLED : **Event:** PaymentFailedEvent
AWAITING_WEBHOOK --> CONTRACT_CANCELLED : **Event:** PaymentFailedEvent

AWAITING_WEBHOOK --> TIMEOUT : 60 min timeout

state TIMEOUT <<Processing>> {
  state "TIMEOUT\n(900)\nWebhook Timeout\n(Fallback)" as TO

  note right of TO
    **Webhook Timeout:**

    No webhook received within 60 minutes.

    Fallback actions:
    1. Poll provider API
    2. Check payment status
    3. Either fulfill or cancel
  end note
}

TIMEOUT --> CONTRACT_FULFILLED : **Event:** PaymentCapturedEvent\n(Polling confirmed)
TIMEOUT --> CONTRACT_CANCELLED : **Event:** OrderCancelledEvent\n(Polling failed)

CONTRACT_CANCELLED --> [*]

note bottom
  **Contract-Order State Machine v2 - Key Changes:**

  **Early Order Creation:**
  Order created after CONTRACT_DRAFT, before CONTRACT_PENDING
  -> Order number assigned immediately
  -> Order visible in admin from start
  -> Customer has reference during payment

  **New State Sequence:**
  BASKET_ACTIVE -> CONTRACT_DRAFT -> NOT_FINISHED -> CONTRACT_PENDING ->
  CONTRACT_READY -> CONTRACT_COMMITTED -> (IN_PROGRESS) -> CONTRACT_FULFILLED

  **After CONTRACT_COMMITTED:**
  External events can trigger:
  - PaymentInitiatedEvent (proceed to payment)
  - OrderCancelledEvent (external cancellation)
  (Beyond this ticket's scope)

  **State Storage:**
  - Contract state: osc_payment_contract.OXSTATE
  - Order state: oxorder.oxtransstatus + osc_payment_order_state.OXPAYMENTSTATE
  - Link: Contract.OXORDERID -> oxorder.OXID (established at NOT_FINISHED)
end note

note as N_FLOW
  **Complete Flow Example (v2):**

  1. User clicks "Place Order"
     -> Contract DRAFT created

  2. Contract draft complete
     -> ORDER CREATED (NOT_FINISHED)
     -> Contract.OXORDERID = order.OXID
     -> Order number assigned

  3. Contract transitions to PENDING
     -> PaymentAuthorizationHandler: Authorize payment
     -> FraudCheckHandler: Check fraud
     -> StockReservationHandler: Reserve stock

  4. All conditions fulfilled
     -> Contract transitions to READY_TO_COMMIT

  5. Contract committed
     -> Contract.OXSTATE = 'committed'

  6. External: PaymentInitiatedEvent
     -> Customer redirected to provider
     -> Order state: IN_PROGRESS (500-800)

  7. Customer completes payment
     -> Order state: AWAITING_WEBHOOK (600)

  8. Webhook received
     -> Contract transitions to FULFILLED
     -> Order state: OK

  **Alternative path at step 6:**
  External: OrderCancelledEvent
     -> Contract cancelled
     -> Order cancelled
end note

@enduml
